## Resolver cascade (@kayamo/food `resolve.ts`) — order is fixed

1. My Foods (the user's own confirmed foods)
2. Curated core (`source='ph_core'`, matched on name and its aliases)
3. Local cache
4. Open Food Facts — jumps to FIRST when a barcode is present
5. USDA FoodData Central

There is **no LLM rung**. A model never produces a nutrition number, and
`llm-nutrition-guard.ts` rejects any LLM schema carrying nutrition keys. The
model's job is to read text and quantities; the numbers come from the cascade.
Label OCR is the one place a model transcribes printed numbers, and the user
confirms them, confidence is capped, and the row is stored
`verified_by_user=false`.

An earlier version of this rule listed an "LLM estimate, last resort" sixth rung.
That contradicted the project constitution and the code that enforces it. The
constitution wins. `resolve.ts` still carries a vestigial `LlmEstimate` hook with
no caller; it is scheduled for removal.

Never collapse the cascade into a single model call.
Always return a ranked candidate list, never a bare answer.

A record missing any of the three core macros is excluded, not filled with
zeroes. Energy without an explicit per-100g basis is excluded too.

## Licensing — hard constraints

- Do NOT scrape FNRI PhilFCT or any FNRI endpoint. No open licence exists.
  Curated core values come from ingredient decomposition of CC0 USDA data, with
  the assumption recorded in `source_note`.
- Open Food Facts is ODbL: store the attribution with every imported record and
  surface it. Send a reachable contact in the User-Agent and respect the
  published rate limit.
- USDA FoodData Central is CC0 — free to use. Its `foodNutrients` are already
  per 100 g, including branded foods. Do not convert by serving size.

## Portions

Offer the units that fit the food and the viewer's locale. Filipino units
(tasa, piraso, order, hiwa, kutsara, bowl) remain first-class for Filipino
dishes; they are no longer the default ordering for every picker, because the
product is global. Grams are always available.

Vague sizes (large / right-sized / small, malaki / sakto / maliit) map to portion
multipliers, never ignored.
